## Proactive Co-Director — Complete ✅

### Backend

**`studio-backend/app/services/proactive_codirector_service.py`**
- `ProactiveCheck` Pydantic model: `should_surface`, `message`, `trigger_type`, `save_to_notes`
- `ProactiveCoDirectorService` — all heuristic, no LLM, no blocking I/O:
  - `check_scene_save()` — 3 checks in priority order:
    1. **Motif gap** — same emotional tone 4+ consecutive scenes → surfaces with tonal advice
    2. **Continuity break** — INT/DAY → EXT/NIGHT jump without bridge → flags it
    3. **Character continuity** — shared character across conflicting locations → flags it
  - `check_project_open()` — gap > 48h → re-orientation note with scene count + approved count; fires **once per session** per project (in-memory guard)
  - `check_cut_assembly()` — audience simulation: tonal arc, protagonist presence, location variety; deduped by **cut hash** (only fires when approved scenes change)
- Silent by default — `should_surface: False` unless something meaningful found

**`studio-backend/app/routes/proactive.py`**
- `POST /api/f51/studio/projects/{id}/co-director/proactive-check`
- Validates trigger type, routes to correct service method
- **Fail-silent** — any exception returns `should_surface: False`, never blocks user

**`studio-backend/main.py`** — `proactive_router` registered

### Frontend

**`studio-app/src/hooks/useProactiveCoDirector.ts`**
- `check(triggerType, options?)` — calls backend, sets card state if `should_surface: true`
- `dismiss()` — clears card + writes `sessionStorage` key → never re-appears in same session
- `saveToNotes(onSaved?)` — dismisses + calls optional callback

**`studio-app/src/components/ProactiveCoDirectorCard.tsx`**
- Dark card, 3px teal left border
- `CO-DIRECTOR` eyebrow in teal 9px + trigger label
- Message in co-director voice
- `×` dismiss button (top-right)
- "Save to Notes" button (teal, only when `save_to_notes: true`)
- Inline — never modal, never toast

### Triggers wired:
| Trigger | Location | When |
|---|---|---|
| `scene_save` | `WritersRoom.tsx` | After `updateScene` or `createScene` succeeds |
| `project_open` | `ProjectWorkspace.tsx` | On `ProjectWorkspaceBody` mount |
| `cut_assembly` | `ScreeningRoom.tsx` | On mount when `activeProjectId` is set |

