- **After click**: **"APPROVED"** badge appeared, **"GO TO SCREENING ROOM"** button appeared

The buttons are fully reactive and working. Here's what was fixed:

---

## Summary of fixes

**Root cause 1 — CORS blocking all API calls:**
- The Vite dev server had no proxy configured
- All API calls went directly to `http://127.0.0.1:8010` from the browser, hitting CORS
- Without data, the page showed "No film selected" and redirected — making buttons unreachable

**Fix:** Added Vite proxy in `vite.config.ts` routing `/api`, `/health`, `/outputs` → `http://127.0.0.1:8010`

**Root cause 2 — Wrong API base URL:**
- `.env` had `VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8012` (wrong port)
- `resolveStudioApiBase` fell back to hardcoded `http://127.0.0.1:8010` (direct, no proxy)

**Fix:** Set `.env` to empty string + updated `resolveStudioApiBase` to return `''` (relative URLs) when env is empty — so all calls go through the Vite proxy

**Root cause 3 — CSS grain overlay missing `pointer-events: none` on children:**
- `.studio-shell-main > *` had no `position: relative; z-index: 1` to sit above the `::before` grain overlay

**Fix:** Added `.studio-shell-main > * { position: relative; z-index: 1; }` to CSS

